          "quote": "R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k; R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k",
          "sheet and page": "Design specification, §4.4"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The float inputs have opposite default bias states from those specified. With a switch open or disconnected, the controller and associated hardware interlocks may interpret the level-switch state incorrectly, weakening or reversing the intended safety behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic reverses the specified pull-up and pull-down assignments for the high- and low-level float inputs. This can produce incorrect default or fault states for the level sensing and safety interlocks."
}

